Q = (0,0);
R = (1,0);
P = (1.1,0.5);
SS = 0.6*P;
T = R + 0.6*(P-R);
draw(T--SS--P--R--Q--SS);
label("$P$",P,N);
label("$S$",SS,NW);
label("$Q$",Q,S);
label("$R$",R,S);
label("$T$",T,ENE);
[/asy]

candidate_final_content:
Since \(PQ=QR\), the median \(\overline{QM}\) is also an altitude to \(\overline{PR}\). Thus \(PM=\frac{PR}{2}=16\).

In right triangle \(PQM\):
\[
QM=\sqrt{PQ^2-PM^2}
=\sqrt{34^2-16^2}
=\sqrt{1156-256}
=\sqrt{900}
=30.
\]

\[
\boxed{30}
\]

